wlan_mt: STA mgmt_tx and testmode_cmd take the 3.17 cfg80211 arguments

The driver picks op signatures by LINUX_VERSION_CODE, which is the host
kernel's 3.10, while backports 3.17 cfg80211 calls the ops with its own
argument lists. The P2P ops already have CONFIG_MTK_BENTEN_SUPPORT variants
for that; the STA ones were missed:

  testmode_cmd(wiphy, wdev, data, len)       driver took (wiphy, data, len)
  mgmt_tx(wiphy, wdev, params, cookie)       driver took the 3.10 list

testmode_cmd treated the wireless_dev as its parameter block and cleared the
top byte of wdev->wiphy; mgmt_tx read buf, len and cookie from the stack and
wrote the cookie through that pointer. The remaining incompatible-pointer
warnings on the station ops are const-only (u8 *mac vs const u8 *mac).

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/mt_soc/conn_soc/mt_wifi/wlan/os/linux/include/gl_cfg80211.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/mt_soc/conn_soc/mt_wifi/wlan/os/linux/include/gl_cfg80211.h
@@ -336,7 +336,15 @@
     );
 
 
